  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Multisectoral National Strategic Plan for TB Control 2017-2021 (PENMTB) in El Salvador - El Salvador (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Salvador, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Republic of El Salvador (MOH)This program has the following goals: Early detection of tuberculosis, reduction of mortality and initiation of the process of Advanced Control and Pre-Elimination of TB as a public health problem in selected municipalities, applying the WHO Post-2015 Strategy at national level with multi-sector support and involvement. The objectives of this program are: Detect at least 90% of respiratory symptomatic patients prioritizing municipalities that have the greatest detection gap..  Detect at least 90% of tuberculosis cases prioritizing municipalities that have the greatest detection gap..  Cure over 90% of cases of positive bacteriological pulmonary TB..  Detect at least 90% of the bacteriologically confirmed cases of drug-resistant tuberculosis (tuberculosis resistant to Rifampicin and/or multi-drug-resistant tuberculosis) reported to the national tuberculosis program..  Achieve 90% success rate in treatment of cases of drug-resistant TB..  Reduce the percentage of deaths by TB/HIV coinfection by 5 percentage points compared to 2012 (19%)..  Make the End TB Strategy operational in 100% of the services of the National Health System, prisons and other high-risk populations..  Achieve a TB incidence rate of between 19 and 15 x 100,000 inhabitants in at least 50% of the municipalities classified in pre-elimination..  Reduce the mortality rate for TB in the country from 0.5 per 100,000 inhabitants to 0.4 per 100,000 inhabitants (20% reduction).</narrative>
  </description>
